# UI Component Standards

## Back Navigation — Always Use `BackToHubButton`

Any button that navigates back to the hub or a parent view MUST use `BackToHubButton`.
Never create a custom back button with `ArrowLeft` + inline Tailwind.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom back button
import { ArrowLeft } from 'lucide-react'
<button onClick={onBack} className="p-2 rounded-lg ...">
  <ArrowLeft className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>

// ✅ GOOD
import BackToHubButton from '@/components/ui/BackToHubButton'
<BackToHubButton onClick={onBack} />

// ✅ GOOD — custom label for non-hub destinations
<BackToHubButton onClick={onBack} label="Back to Inbox" />
```

`ArrowLeft` from lucide-react is only acceptable inside multi-step form wizard "Previous" buttons — not for page navigation.

---

## Cards — Always Use `Card` or `BlockCard`

Never use raw `<div>` with custom border/background/shadow classes as a card container.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-lg p-6">

// ✅ GOOD — general content card
import Card from '@/components/ui/Card'
<Card variant="elevated">

// ✅ GOOD — composable hub block
import BlockCard from '@/components/ui/BlockCard'
<BlockCard icon={ClipboardList} title="DOT Application" status="in-progress">
```

---

## In-App Panels — Always Use `HubSectionPanel` + `BlockCard variant="embed"`

**This is the unique "block/vault" chrome of the app** (rim glow, accent strip, chamfer, sheen). Any page or surface that renders a first-class content panel MUST use it — not just the Hub. Simple Mode, employer screens, dashboards, admin pages, and any future feature all follow this pattern so the product feels like one app, not a patchwork.

**Pattern:**

```tsx
import HubSectionPanel from '@/components/hub/HubSectionPanel'
import BlockCard from '@/components/ui/BlockCard'

<HubSectionPanel isDark={isDark} accent='teal'>
  <BlockCard
    variant='embed'
    icon={Briefcase}
    title='Find jobs'
    description='Pick a role — Stormi will shape your career card around it.'
    headerActions={<Button size='sm'>Filters</Button>}
  >
    {/* content */}
  </BlockCard>
</HubSectionPanel>
```

**Accent colors** (`VaultAccentPreset`) — stay consistent across the app:

| Accent    | Use for                                                        |
|-----------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| `teal`    | Default — blocks, career card, job rail, primary content       |
| `violet`  | Stormi (AI), co-pilot surfaces                                 |
| `sky`     | Job alerts, selected-job context, referenceable external data  |
| `amber`   | Employer requests, saved items, warning/attention surfaces     |
| `indigo`  | STORM balance, tokenomics, identity / on-chain surfaces        |

### When a `BlockCard` header is the wrong shape

Some surfaces (a scrolling rail, a job detail with custom title chrome, an entire employer dashboard tab) don't fit `BlockCard`'s fixed `icon + title + description` header. In those cases, use `HubSectionPanel` alone and render a matching inline header — same teal/violet/etc. tinted icon tile + title/description text:

```tsx
<HubSectionPanel isDark={isDark} accent='teal' contentClassName='flex flex-col h-full min-h-0'>
  <div className='flex items-start gap-3 pb-3 mb-3 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-gray-700/50'>
    <div className='flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-teal-50 dark:bg-teal-500/15 text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-200 ring-1 ring-teal-200 dark:ring-teal-400/30'>
      <Briefcase className='h-4 w-4' />
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 className='text-sm font-semibold'>Find jobs</h3>
      <p className='text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-gray-400'>Pick a role.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {/* scrolling content */}
</HubSectionPanel>
```

**NEVER** do:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — loses the vault chrome; product starts to feel like a different app
<div className="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm p-4">
  <h3>Section title</h3>
  {/* ... */}
</div>
```

**Reference implementations:**
- [`CandidateHub.tsx`](src/components/hub/CandidateHub.tsx) — every hub section
- [`SimpleCardPanel.tsx`](src/components/simple/SimpleCardPanel.tsx) — Simple Mode right column (violet Stormi + teal career card + violet chat drawer)
- [`SimpleJobDetailPanel.tsx`](src/components/simple/SimpleJobDetailPanel.tsx) — sky-accent panel with inline custom header
- [`SimpleJobRail.tsx`](src/components/simple/SimpleJobRail.tsx) — teal rail using the inline-header escape hatch

