## Modals — Always Use `Modal` (NEVER hand-roll overlays)

Every overlay/dialog/picker in this app MUST use the shared `Modal` component from `@/components/ui/Modal`. This is **non-negotiable** because `Modal` handles three things that hand-rolled `fixed inset-0` divs always forget:

1. **Scroll lock** — sets `body.style.overflow = 'hidden'` on mount so the page behind doesn't scroll. Uses a nested-modal counter so the lock only lifts when the last modal closes.
2. **Portal** — uses `createPortal(content, document.body)` so the modal is outside every parent stacking context. This prevents the navbar or other `z-index` layers from rendering on top.
3. **z-index** — accepts a `zIndex` prop (default 1000). Nested modals just pass a higher value.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hand-rolled overlay (WILL have scroll bleed + navbar z-index issues)
<div className="fixed inset-0 z-[70] flex items-center justify-center">
  <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-black/50" onClick={onClose} />
  <div className="relative bg-white rounded-2xl max-w-2xl">
    {/* content */}
  </div>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — use Modal + ModalHeader
import Modal, { ModalHeader } from '@/components/ui/Modal'

<Modal onClose={onClose} maxWidth="max-w-2xl">
  <ModalHeader title="Add Tools" subtitle="Pick industry-specific tools" onClose={onClose} />
  <div className="p-4">
    {/* content */}
  </div>
</Modal>
```

### If you think you need a custom overlay

You don't. The only exception is `LoadingScreen` (full-page takeover with no close button). Every other overlay — pickers, confirmations, previews, forms — goes through `Modal`.

### Checklist for new modals

- [ ] Uses `<Modal>` component (not `fixed inset-0`)
- [ ] Uses `<ModalHeader>` for title + close button (not a custom header)
- [ ] Sets `zIndex` if it can open on top of another modal
- [ ] Does NOT manually set `body.style.overflow` (Modal handles it)
- [ ] Does NOT use `createPortal` directly (Modal handles it)

### Hub-aligned modal chrome (`panelShape="block"`)

Feature modals tied to the composable hub — block picker, Stormi walkthroughs, block-category flows — must use **block shell** styling so they match the hub vault, not generic SaaS `rounded-2xl` dialogs:

- Pass **`panelShape="block"`** on `<Modal>` — same outer shell as hub category cards (`rounded-xl border`, teal `ring-1`, muted fill). See `Modal.tsx` and `BlockPickerModal`.
- When using **`ModalHeader`**, pass **`variant="block"`** so the sticky header aligns with that shell.
- **Custom headers** (e.g. avatar + title) are fine if they reuse the same border/background tokens as `ModalHeader variant="block"` — stay visually consistent with hub blocks.

For **in-hub panels** (not portaled modals), use **`HubSectionPanel` + `BlockCard`** — never a raw `div` with ad-hoc `rounded-2xl border shadow-lg` card styling.

**Reference implementation:** [`StormiWalkthrough.tsx`](src/components/hub/StormiWalkthrough.tsx) — `Modal` `panelShape="block"` with zero extra hand-rolled header chrome; inner content is `HubSectionPanel` + `BlockCard variant="embed"` (violet accent for Stormi). [`BlockPickerModal.tsx`](src/components/hub/BlockPickerModal.tsx) uses `panelShape="block"` + `ModalHeader variant="block"`.

